cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results, please cite this repository and the Lean name of the result you use."
type: software
title: "Fugue — machine-checked proofs (Lean 4 / Mathlib)"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 proofs, checked against Mathlib, of the mathematics behind the HSLN exploration
  (2026): theta series of E8 and E8 ⊕ E8 (Θ_E8 = E₄, 240σ₃(n) and 480σ₇(n) vectors), Witt's
  D16⁺ isospectrality, Ramanujan's congruences τ(n) ≡ σ₁₁(n) (mod 691) and p(5n+4) ≡ 0 (mod 5),
  Jacobi's two-square theorem, L(1, χ₋₄) = π/4, the Cauchy and Dirichlet rings, Euler-factor
  composition, Hecke's functional equations for Eisenstein series, and a library on zero-free
  regions of the Riemann zeta function. No sorry; only Lean's standard axioms.
authors:
  - family-names: Morley-Smith
    given-names: Richard
repository-code: "https://github.com/rmorleysmith/fugue-formal"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - modular forms
  - E8 lattice
  - theta series
  - Eisenstein series
  - Dirichlet series
  - Riemann zeta function
